{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Wdbg7ULmP1G65yda2aSJSY","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\ttitle: Coding Session\n3\ttype: schema\n4\tentity: CodingSession\n5\tversion: 1\n6\tschema:\n7\t  summary?: string, one-paragraph what happened in this coding session\n8\t  changed_file?(array): string, files created, edited, deleted, or inspected\n9\t  verification?(array): string, checks run and their result\n10\t  decision?(array): string, decisions surfaced or created during the session\n11\t  blocker?(array): string, unresolved blockers or failed approaches\n12\t  next_step?(array): string, explicit cursor for the next coding session\n13\t  produced?(array): Entity, notes or artifacts created or updated\n14\tsettings:\n15\t  validation: warn\n16\t  frontmatter:\n17\t    project: string, the Basic Memory project this session belongs to\n18\t    started: string, when the session began or checkpoint was created\n19\t    repository: string, stable repository identifier such as owner/name\n20\t    repo_root: string, Git repository root for this checkout\n21\t    cwd: string, working directory for the session\n22\t    branch: string, checked-out Git branch or HEAD when detached\n23\t    git_sha: string, exact Git commit at checkpoint time\n24\t    ended?: string, when the session was checkpointed\n25\t    status?(enum, lifecycle of the checkpoint): [open, resumed, closed]\n26\t    pull_request_number?: string, current pull request number as a queryable identifier\n27\t    pull_request_title?: string, current pull request title\n28\t    pull_request_url?: string, canonical pull request URL\n29\t    pull_request_state?(enum, pull request state at checkpoint time): [open, closed, merged]\n30\t    pull_request_base?: string, pull request base branch\n31\t    pull_request_head?: string, pull request head branch\n32\t    username?: string, operating-system user that created the checkpoint\n33\t    hostname?: string, host that created the checkpoint\n34\t    session_id?: string, exact host-provided session identifier (pair with agent)\n35\t    agent?: string, agent harness identifier such as tau or claude-code or codex\n36\t    tau_session_id?: string, legacy Tau session identifier (read compatibility only)\n37\t    claude_session_id?: string, legacy Claude Code session identifier (read compatibility only)\n38\t    codex_session_id?: string, legacy Codex session identifier (read compatibility only)\n39\t    codex_turn_id?: string, Codex turn identifier\n40\t    trigger?: string, compaction trigger or deliberate checkpoint source\n41\t    model?: string, active model slug when known\n42\t    capture?(enum, how this checkpoint was produced): [extractive, deliberate, summarized]\n43\t---\n44\t\n45\t# Coding Session\n46\t\n47\tA **CodingSession** is a resumable engineering checkpoint whose repository\n48\tidentity is structured and queryable. Required Git fields make it possible to\n49\tfind the exact work cursor without parsing prose.\n50\t\n51\tExamples:\n52\t\n53\t`bm_search(note_types=[\"coding_session\"], filters={\"repository\": \"owner/repo\"})`\n54\t\n55\t`bm_search(note_types=[\"coding_session\"], filters={\"pull_request_number\": \"123\"})`\n56\t\n57\t`bm_search(note_types=[\"coding_session\"], filters={\"agent\": \"codex\", \"session_id\": \"<id>\"})`\n58\t\n59\tPull-request fields are optional because valid coding work can precede a pull\n60\trequest. When a pull request exists, checkpoint writers populate the complete\n61\tpull-request field set. Multiple checkpoints from one agent chat share the\n62\t`agent` and `session_id` pair; session IDs alone are not cross-agent identity.\n63\tEach new checkpoint can link to its verified predecessor with\n64\t`continues [[Previous checkpoint title]]`. New writers use the shared fields.\n65\tLegacy agent-specific session fields remain accepted for existing notes; do not\n66\trewrite old checkpoints or infer missing session IDs.\n67\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"70820d22-2e57-4bbb-bd59-bfa55fb4a23c","uuid":"67b237ab-08c5-433c-b149-b59a6f0c1b9e","timestamp":"2026-11-03T23:49:34.933Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/runner/work/_temp/basic-memory/plugins/claude-code/schemas/coding-session.md","content":"---\ntitle: Coding Session\ntype: schema\nentity: CodingSession\nversion: 1\nschema:\n  summary?: string, one-paragraph what happened in this coding session\n  changed_file?(array): string, files created, edited, deleted, or inspected\n  verification?(array): string, checks run and their result\n  decision?(array): string, decisions surfaced or created during the session\n  blocker?(array): string, unresolved blockers or failed approaches\n  next_step?(array): string, explicit cursor for the next coding session\n  produced?(array): Entity, notes or artifacts created or updated\nsettings:\n  validation: warn\n  frontmatter:\n    project: string, the Basic Memory project this session belongs to\n    started: string, when the session began or checkpoint was created\n    repository: string, stable repository identifier such as owner/name\n    repo_root: string, Git repository root for this checkout\n    cwd: string, working directory for the session\n    branch: string, checked-out Git branch or HEAD when detached\n    git_sha: string, exact Git commit at checkpoint time\n    ended?: string, when the session was checkpointed\n    status?(enum, lifecycle of the checkpoint): [open, resumed, closed]\n    pull_request_number?: string, current pull request number as a queryable identifier\n    pull_request_title?: string, current pull request title\n    pull_request_url?: string, canonical pull request URL\n    pull_request_state?(enum, pull request state at checkpoint time): [open, closed, merged]\n    pull_request_base?: string, pull request base branch\n    pull_request_head?: string, pull request head branch\n    username?: string, operating-system user that created the checkpoint\n    hostname?: string, host that created the checkpoint\n    session_id?: string, exact host-provided session identifier (pair with agent)\n    agent?: string, agent harness identifier such as tau or claude-code or codex\n    tau_session_id?: string, legacy Tau session identifier (read compatibility only)\n    claude_session_id?: string, legacy Claude Code session identifier (read compatibility only)\n    codex_session_id?: string, legacy Codex session identifier (read compatibility only)\n    codex_turn_id?: string, Codex turn identifier\n    trigger?: string, compaction trigger or deliberate checkpoint source\n    model?: string, active model slug when known\n    capture?(enum, how this checkpoint was produced): [extractive, deliberate, summarized]\n---\n\n# Coding Session\n\nA **CodingSession** is a resumable engineering checkpoint whose repository\nidentity is structured and queryable. Required Git fields make it possible to\nfind the exact work cursor without parsing prose.\n\nExamples:\n\n`bm_search(note_types=[\"coding_session\"], filters={\"repository\": \"owner/repo\"})`\n\n`bm_search(note_types=[\"coding_session\"], filters={\"pull_request_number\": \"123\"})`\n\n`bm_search(note_types=[\"coding_session\"], filters={\"agent\": \"codex\", \"session_id\": \"<id>\"})`\n\nPull-request fields are optional because valid coding work can precede a pull\nrequest. When a pull request exists, checkpoint writers populate the complete\npull-request field set. Multiple checkpoints from one agent chat share the\n`agent` and `session_id` pair; session IDs alone are not cross-agent identity.\nEach new checkpoint can link to its verified predecessor with\n`continues [[Previous checkpoint title]]`. New writers use the shared fields.\nLegacy agent-specific session fields remain accepted for existing notes; do not\nrewrite old checkpoints or infer missing session IDs.\n","numLines":67,"startLine":1,"totalLines":67}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Wdbg7ULmP1G65yda2aSJSY","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Hdku4ZyeKdycqJGt6YxiLG","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\ttitle: Decision\n3\ttype: schema\n4\tentity: Decision\n5\tversion: 1\n6\tschema:\n7\t  decision: string, the choice that was made\n8\t  rationale?: string, why this choice over the alternatives\n9\t  alternative?(array): string, options that were considered and not taken\n10\t  consequence?(array): string, what this decision commits us to\n11\t  context?: string, the situation that prompted the decision\n12\t  affects?(array): Entity, work or notes this decision bears on\n13\t  supersedes?: Entity, a prior decision this one replaces\n14\tsettings:\n15\t  validation: warn\n16\t  frontmatter:\n17\t    status?(enum, lifecycle of the decision): [open, accepted, superseded, rejected]\n18\t    decided?: string, when the decision was made (ISO timestamp)\n19\t    project?: string, the Basic Memory project this decision belongs to\n20\t---\n21\t\n22\t# Decision\n23\t\n24\tA **DecisionNote** is a durable record of a real choice — one with alternatives\n25\tand a rationale, not a passing preference. Basic Memory host integrations\n26\tencourage agents to capture these as decisions are made or explicitly requested.\n27\t\n28\tDecisions are found by structured recall:\n29\t`bm_search(filters={\"type\": \"decision\", \"status\": \"open\"})`.\n30\t\n31\t## What makes a good DecisionNote\n32\t\n33\t- **decision** — state the choice plainly.\n34\t- **rationale** + **alternative** — why this, and what was rejected. This is the\n35\t  part that saves a future session from relitigating the same ground.\n36\t- **consequence** — what the choice commits the work to.\n37\t- **affects** / **supersedes** — relations that wire the decision into the graph.\n38\t\n39\t## Frontmatter\n40\t\n41\t`type: decision` plus `status` make decisions queryable. Capture decisions\n42\tsparingly — one note per genuine decision, not per opinion. Validation is `warn`,\n43\tnever blocking.\n44\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"70820d22-2e57-4bbb-bd59-bfa55fb4a23c","uuid":"d3fd7534-1485-4c37-b9e0-6c133fbb9501","timestamp":"2026-11-03T23:49:34.936Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/runner/work/_temp/basic-memory/plugins/claude-code/schemas/decision.md","content":"---\ntitle: Decision\ntype: schema\nentity: Decision\nversion: 1\nschema:\n  decision: string, the choice that was made\n  rationale?: string, why this choice over the alternatives\n  alternative?(array): string, options that were considered and not taken\n  consequence?(array): string, what this decision commits us to\n  context?: string, the situation that prompted the decision\n  affects?(array): Entity, work or notes this decision bears on\n  supersedes?: Entity, a prior decision this one replaces\nsettings:\n  validation: warn\n  frontmatter:\n    status?(enum, lifecycle of the decision): [open, accepted, superseded, rejected]\n    decided?: string, when the decision was made (ISO timestamp)\n    project?: string, the Basic Memory project this decision belongs to\n---\n\n# Decision\n\nA **DecisionNote** is a durable record of a real choice — one with alternatives\nand a rationale, not a passing preference. Basic Memory host integrations\nencourage agents to capture these as decisions are made or explicitly requested.\n\nDecisions are found by structured recall:\n`bm_search(filters={\"type\": \"decision\", \"status\": \"open\"})`.\n\n## What makes a good DecisionNote\n\n- **decision** — state the choice plainly.\n- **rationale** + **alternative** — why this, and what was rejected. This is the\n  part that saves a future session from relitigating the same ground.\n- **consequence** — what the choice commits the work to.\n- **affects** / **supersedes** — relations that wire the decision into the graph.\n\n## Frontmatter\n\n`type: decision` plus `status` make decisions queryable. Capture decisions\nsparingly — one note per genuine decision, not per opinion. Validation is `warn`,\nnever blocking.\n","numLines":44,"startLine":1,"totalLines":44}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Hdku4ZyeKdycqJGt6YxiLG","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
